                <pb facs="0171" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/564.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Bishop Brent.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon informs him that consuls general of Austria and Italy, Bernauer and
                    Faraone, appointed delegates to opium commission, and that China has delegated
                    Tao-t’ao Liu Yii-lin, Tao-t’ai Kwan Ching-hsien, and T’ang Kai-sun.</p>
            </div>
